<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $934 mln in April 16 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $934 mln in April 16 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $934 million to $46,013 million in the week ended April 16, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $933 million to $46,277 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $5,110 million to $845,664 million.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
